{"title":"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangle</a> with a diagonal of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is twice as long as it is wide. What is the area of the rectangle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6ed218db58489de6996140305c64e0a69e2b180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\mathrm {A}) \\ \\frac 14x^2 \\qquad (\\mathrm {B}) \\ \\frac 25x^2 \\qquad (\\mathrm {C})\\ \\frac 12x^2 \\qquad (\\mathrm {D}) \\ x^2 \\qquad (\\mathrm {E})\\ \\frac 32x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"437\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be the width, so the length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/f/a4ff082ac4c9ee59c97a78e5b5d445c75f1a2a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/b/00be581a6e6f8323e90c61d02376b223a592d591.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w^2 + 4w^2 = x^2 \\Longrightarrow \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{5}} = w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"220\" height=\"37\" />. The area of the rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/c/9fc5e6bd9d9410a0a46e974adc925bff06c4b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(w)(2w) = 2w^2 = 2\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{5}}\\right)^2 = \\frac{2}{5}x^2 \\ \\mathrm{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"303\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A\">2005 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a